<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka to get $103 mln Kuwaiti development aid.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka to get $103 mln Kuwaiti development aid.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuwaiti government has agreed to give $103 million to Sri Lanka as aid to conduct feasibility studies for two proposed irrigation schemes and to rehabilitate 28 bridges, the state-owned Daily News said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The funding, allocated through the Kuwait Fund for Economic Development, was assured during a two-day visit to Kuwait by Sri Lankan President Chandrika Kumaratunga, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It added that the fund's Deputy Director General, Abdulwahab Al-Bader, assured Kumaratunga the feasibility studies on the two irrigation schemes, estimated to cost $93 million, would begin soon.</p>
<p>Kuwait has already contributed $75 million towards development projects in Sri Lanka, it said.</p>
</text>
